  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 235 PM EDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nWe will remain on the eastern periphery of an anomalous upper level \nridge centered across the central CONUS through the period. A trough \nwill also translate atop the northern Great Lakes and into the New \nEngland Region mid/late week to assist in moderating temps to only\na few degrees above normal locally. The associated high pressure \nand subsidence aloft will also promote clear skies and drier air.\nThese dry/clear conditions will allow for cool mornings but very \npleasant afternoons. The favorable radiational cooling may also \nallow for some patchy valley fog, and perhaps isolated frost in \nsheltered valleys across far NE TN/SW VA and the higher terrain \neach morning as well. Overall, a very comfortable weather pattern\nlacking significant impacts for the foreseeable future.",
